==English==
[[File:Syntrichia papillosa.jpg|right|thumb|Gemmae on a leaf tip of ''Syntrichia papillosa'']]

===Etymology===
{{lbor|en|la|gemma|t=bud on a plant}}. {{dbt|en|gem|Gemma}}.

===Noun===
{{en-noun|gemmae}}

# {{lb|en|biology}} An [[asexual#Adjective|asexual]] [[reproductive]] [[structure#Noun|structure]], as found in [[animal]]s such as [[hydra]] ([[genus]] ''[[Hydra]]'') and [[plant#Noun|plants]] such as [[liverwort]]s ([[division]] [[Marchantiophyta]]), [[consist]]ing of a [[cluster#Noun|cluster]] of [[cell#Noun|cells]] from which [[new#Adjective|new]] [[individual#Noun|individuals]] can [[develop]]; a [[bud#Noun|bud]].
#: {{synonyms|en|q1=archaic|gemmule}}
#* '''1969''', Rudolf Mathias Schuster, ''The Hepaticae and Anthocerotae of North America East of the Hundredth Meridian'', Volume 1, Columbia University Press, [https://books.google.com.au/books?id=830MAQAAMAAJ&q=%22gemmae%22&dq=%22gemmae%22&hl=en&sa=X&redir_esc=y page 527],
#*: I know of no other genera with such intramarginal formation of true '''gemmae'''.
#* '''1990''', Anthony John Edwin Smith, ''The Liverworts of Britain and Ireland'', [https://books.google.com.au/books?id=TdJxDOXxX18C&pg=PA2&dq=%22gemmae%22&hl=en&sa=X&redir_esc=y#v=onepage&q=%22gemmae%22&f=false page 2],
#*: '''Gemmae''' are frequently longer than wide or of irregular shape.
#*: According to Degenkolbe, '''gemmae'''-bearing leaves are always different in form from normal leaves.
#* '''2005''', R. N. Chopra, ''Biology of Bryophytes'', [https://books.google.com.au/books?id=zYj4Re6VNc0C&pg=PA32&dq=%22gemmae%22&hl=en&sa=X&redir_esc=y#v=onepage&q=%22gemmae%22&f=false page 32],
#*: In ''Marchantia polymorpha'', high temperature promotes germination of '''gemmae''' (Dacknowski, 1907), and heat absorbed by the '''gemmae''' accelerates their germination (Fitting, 1942).

